0,Somyev language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Somyev_language,"Language family. Niger–Congo?Somyev (Somyewe), also known as Kila (""blacksmith"" in Fulfulde), is a nearly extinct Mambiloid language of two villages, one in Nigeria and one in Cameroon, that is spoken by a caste of blacksmiths that live among the Mambila.",Somyev,Niger-Congo
1,Somyev language,https://grokipedia.com/page/somyev_language,"Somyev, also known as Sombə or Somyewe, is a severely endangered Mambiloid language of the Niger-Congo family, traditionally spoken exclusively by the Somyewe people—a distinct blacksmith caste—in small enclaves along the Nigeria-Cameroon borderland.",Somyev,Niger-Congo
2,Somyev Language (KGT) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kgt/,Somyev is an endangered indigenous language of Nigeria. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. The language is used as a first language by the elderly only. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Somyev,Niger-Congo
